I looked in the source for 3.1.1 about wishing for artifacts and it appears that
you cannot wish for your own character's quest artifact at all (some people have
stated that this can really screw up your game anyway).  As for wishing for other
artifacts (other character's quest artifacts or weapons) it will work, sometimes.

The formula is something like this: 

chance_to_get_artifact = 2 / (number_of_artifacts_already_existing)

This means the more artifacts you have, the less chance a wish will work.  If
you have less than two artifacts than it will always work.

If you fail the chance, than you get the message:

"For a moment, you feel something in your hands, but it disappears!"

and the wish is used up!

So if you have a lot of artifacts (say 4 or more) it's just not a good risk
to wish for an artifact.  And usually by the time you have a wish to spare
most people already have 8 or 9 artifacts.  Of course that 
"blessed platinum yendorian express card" is pretty darn useful.  Almost makes
me want to play a tourist just to get it on an actual quest.

Please note that once the artifact exists there is no way to remove it from the
count of existing artifacts.  So that cruddy dagger named "Sting" may actually
hurt you in the end.

